Description: Build flite's shared libraries on BSD targets
 configure sets SHFLAGS=-fPIC, which is what turns on flite's shared
 libraries (config/common_make_rules and main/Makefile test `ifdef SHFLAGS`),
 only for Linux, GNU and Solaris targets. On a *-freebsd target it is left
 empty and --enable-shared builds static archives only. Add BSD to the Linux
 case, as FreeBSD's port does. Applied to the generated configure only, as the
 port does, so make never sees configure.in newer than configure.
Origin: FreeBSD port audio/flite, files/patch-configure (first hunk), used as
 a reference
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -4213,7 +4213,7 @@
 
 if test "$shared" = true; then
    case "$target_os" in
-	linux*|k*bsd*-gnu|gnu*)
+	linux*|k*bsd*-gnu|gnu*|*bsd*)
 		SHFLAGS="-fPIC"
         ;;
 	solaris*)
